Data that is not under the MIT licence

The MIT licence above covers the code. The data files below are not MIT: each
value keeps the terms of the source it comes from, and nothing here relicenses
it. Each data folder's LICENSE.md says exactly what it covers, with the full
credits and citations. Space Maps is run as a non-commercial, educational
project; see "Before any commercial use" below.

1. Derived from OpenNGC (Credits: Mattia Verga
   https://github.com/mattiaverga/OpenNGC), licensed under the Creative Commons
   Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0,
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/):

     frontend/data/objects/nebulae/          backend/data/sources/nebulae/
     frontend/data/objects/galaxies/         backend/data/sources/galaxies/
     frontend/data/objects/smbh-curated/     (black holes placed at their
                                              OpenNGC galaxies' centres)

2. Gaia values, distributed by ESA under CC BY-NC 3.0 IGO
   (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/3.0/igo/), "Credit:
   ESA/Gaia/DPAC":
     - frontend/data/objects/bh-curated/ and
       backend/data/sources/bh-curated/gaia-dr3-companions.csv (the seven
       black-hole companions' Gaia DR3 values);
     - frontend/data/objects/nea-exoplanets/ and
       backend/data/sources/nea-exoplanets/ (Gaia DR3 ids, positions and
       G magnitudes of exoplanet hosts);
     - the planetary-nebula distances and central-star ids in the nebulae
       folders (Chornay & Walton 2021, from Gaia EDR3 parallaxes);
     - the HII-region distances in the nebulae folders that Shen et al. 2025
       derive from Gaia DR3 parallaxes of the regions' exciting stars (their
       maser-parallax rows are not Gaia values);
     - the Milky Way glow image, frontend/data/milkyway.webp (NASA/GSFC
       Scientific Visualization Studio, Deep Star Maps 2020; "Gaia DR2:
       ESA/Gaia/DPAC");
     - frontend/data/objects/hr23-clusters/ and its sources hold Hunt &
       Reffert's cluster values, derived from Gaia DR3, and their member
       lists (frontend/data/objects/hr23-clusters/members/ and
       backend/data/sources/hr23-clusters/members-hr24-*.csv.gz: Gaia DR3
       source ids and membership probabilities, Hunt & Reffert 2024 table 2);
     - the live star layer of the 3D view, queried from Gaia archives at run
       time (not stored in this repository).

3. Cosmicflows-4 (Tully et al. 2023, ApJ 944, 94) distances, used under the
   Extragalactic Distance Database's terms (https://edd.ifa.hawaii.edu/terms.php:
   use and sharing for research and education, with citation of Tully et al.
   2009, AJ 138, 323 and of the catalogue; changed values must say so). They are
   in the galaxies and smbh-curated folders, converted from distance moduli by
   Space Maps.

4. Tables served by VizieR (CDS, Strasbourg) are used under VizieR's terms of
   use with their citations: Sharpless, Chornay & Walton, Russeil, Shen et al.
   2025 (nebulae),
   Hunt & Reffert (clusters), UNGC, McConnachie 2012 and Cosmicflows-4
   (galaxies).

Before any commercial use

These would have to be removed, replaced or cleared first:
  - the live Gaia star layer (ESA's authorisation, data.licences@esa.int, or a
    different star source);
  - nea-exoplanets and bh-curated: their Gaia DR3 values;
  - nebulae: the Chornay & Walton (Gaia EDR3) planetary-nebula distances and
    Shen et al. 2025's Gaia DR3 HII-region distances; a rebuild without them
    leaves those 59 planetary nebulae direction-only and the HII regions at
    Russeil 2003's or Shen's maser-parallax distances, or direction-only;
  - hr23-clusters, including its members/ folder (Gaia DR3 source ids and
    membership probabilities): whether Hunt & Reffert's Gaia-derived values
    fall under Gaia's non-commercial term;
  - galaxies and smbh-curated: the Cosmicflows-4 distances (EDD's "research and
    education" terms), to be cleared with their authors or replaced;
  - frontend/data/milkyway.webp, built from NASA SVS "Deep Star Maps 2020"
    (Hipparcos-2, Tycho-2 and Gaia DR2 stars): its terms;
  - the nebulae, galaxies and smbh-curated files each combine CC BY-SA 4.0
    OpenNGC data with values under the terms above; those values would have to
    be separated or cleared before relying on CC BY-SA alone.
